  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Seliwanoff reagent<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo></math>Resorcinol<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo></math> Conc. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>]</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Seliwanoff&#39;s test is a chemical test which distinguishes between aldose and ketose sugars. If the sugar contains a ketone group, it is a ketose. If a sugar contains an aldehyde group, it is an aldose.</p><p>&nbsp;Ketoses show red colour with Seliwanoff Reagent.</p>"
